  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Friday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Storms are dying down overnight but \nwill return Friday, although much weaker and more spread out. \nExcessive rainfall remains a marginal threat, along with localized\nflash flooding. \n\nThe upper level trough that has been driving these storms lifts \nout of Nevada for the weekend with southwest flow taking its \nplace. This is expected to mostly cut off the moisture flow and \nresult in a dry weekend. Models still can\u2019t agree on the forecast \nfor next week, with the sticking point being the path of an upper \nlevel low pressure center. The further south solution would see it\nclip northern Nevada and would be a much cooler and potentially \nwetter solution than the one keeping it near the Canadian border, \nhowever it is not clear which solution is more likely at this \ntime.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in showers and\nthunderstorms through Friday. Moderate confidence in a dry \nweekend. Low confidence in the forecast for thunderstorms to \nstart next week. No changes from the NBM.",
